(7605201, 1229146, 179769, '<td valign="top"><br/>Not as complicated as you might think:  I attached a string to the pitcher and looped it around the handle of the box out of sight on the other side so that I could adjust the angle.  The pitcher kept slipping sideways, so I stuck a piece of tape underneath on the other side so it couldn''t be seen.  Voila!  Cup was propped up from behind by a small lens case so that liquid (iced tea) would tilt toward the camera.  <br/> <br/>Thanks to everyone for so many nice comments and votes!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-12-04 08:57:27.</i></td>', 'Not as complicated as you might think:  I attached a string to the pitcher and looped it around the handle of the box out of sight on the other side so that I could adjust the angle.  The pitcher kept slipping sideways, so I stuck a piece of tape underneath on the other side so it couldn''t be seen.  Voila!  Cup was propped up from behind by a small lens case so that liquid (iced tea) would tilt toward the camera.   Thanks to everyone for so many nice comments and votes!', '2018-12-04 08:56:52.000000', '2018-12-04 08:57:27.000000', 0),
